## Run and change logs

Phase {{ phase_num['logging'] }} keeps two hidden, tool-owned lists on the site
before any register is written:

- **{{ sidecar_run_log_title }}** records this run: a start stamp, provenance
  naming the release and schema version the bundle was built from (and what the
  env file supplied, if one was read), and a stop stamp written on every way out
  -- success, abort, or error -- with the outcome and elapsed time. Nothing is
  granted on it beyond what the running operator already holds.
- **{{ sidecar_change_log_title }}** records CHANGES as type-2 rows: list
  creates, renames (old value and new value side by side), and enterprise-reader
  enrolments, each with an effective-from time and the previous row closed out
  with an effective-to time. Rows are insert-only from the deploy's side; the
  enterprise-reader group is granted Read on this list so an external reader can
  collect them without touching the registers.

Both are owned the same way every list here is: by the tool's provenance marker
in the Description, compared whole. A list of the same title that is NOT this
tool's stops the run rather than being written into. Neither list is created
when the bundle was built with `--no-sidecars`, and neither is deleted by
`rollback.js.txt`.
{% if deployment_log_list %}

This bundle also stamps a **central deployment log**: the site
`{{ deployment_log_site }}` and the list `{{ deployment_log_list }}` on it,
shared by every firmfooting application. The script checks three things before
its first stamp -- the site exists, the list exists on it, and this account
holds AddListItems (Contribute or better) on the list -- reading the
permission from the list itself, not the web. Any miss degrades to an INFO
line and the run carries on; the run log on THIS site always holds the record
regardless. The central site and list are never created by a deploy: create
them once with the deploy-central-log sidecar, or override both with
`DBMLSP_DEPLOY_LOG_SITE` / `DBMLSP_DEPLOY_LOG_LIST` (empty disables).
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

