The cross-column sibling of the per-column rules above, stored on the
LIST (ValidationFormula/ValidationMessage) rather than on a field, so it
may reference any column. Shown as the declared condition rather than the
rendered formula: the condition is what was authored, and the SharePoint
syntax carrying it is a renderer detail.

A column rule that compares a date with `today` or `now` is enforced here
rather than on its column, guarded so a blank never fails it, and its
message is joined onto the list's. Measured 2026-09-02: the formula clock
behind TODAY() and NOW() ran 16 to 20 hours behind an AUS Eastern site,
while [Modified] in a list formula is the instant of the save being
validated; a column formula may not reference it.
